      "content": "To address behaviors that appear mischievous or inexplicably erratic, train staff to distinguish between maladaptive symptoms of delirium or psychosis and intentional rule-breaking, as the intervention differs significantly. In these high-confusion scenarios, focus shifting techniques become vital; calmly redirecting the patient's attention to a neutral object or a non-threatening task can often bypass their internal chaos more effectively than logical arguments. It is equally crucial for staff to prioritize personal safety first by utilizing a low-profile defensive stance, avoiding sudden movements, and maintaining a calm demeanor until medical causes for the unpredictability are ruled out.",
